# What NOT to send to the Docker daemon as build context.
#
# Everything in this directory is packed up and shipped to the daemon before a build starts, so an
# ignored file is not merely unused - it is never transferred. This project has ~41 MB of
# node_modules under frontend/, which would be copied on every single build without the line below.

# The frontend is not part of this image.
frontend/

# Build output. The image builds its own inside the build stage; copying a host-built target/ in
# would also make the image depend on whatever JDK happened to be on the developer's machine.
target/
out/

# History and tooling.
.git/
.github/
.idea/
*.iml

# Docker's own files: changing compose.yaml must not invalidate the build cache.
compose.yaml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Local secrets - belt and braces. .env is gitignored, and must never reach an image either.
.env
.env.*

# Documentation and editor noise.
docs/
*.md
.DS_Store
